1️⃣ Fetch the latest branches from GitHub

First make sure your local repo knows about the new branch.

git fetch origin

2️⃣ Switch to the backend-api branch

If the branch exists on GitHub:

git checkout backend-api


If it gives error, use:

git checkout -b backend-api origin/backend-api


This links your local branch with the GitHub branch.

3️⃣ Add your changes

Now stage your files.

git add .

4️⃣ Commit the changes
git commit -m "Backend API implementation"

5️⃣ Push to the backend-api branch
git push origin backend-api


Your code will now go to:

repo
 ├── main
 └── backend-api   ← your code

6️⃣ Later create a Pull Request

On GitHub:

backend-api → main


This merges your backend code into the main project safely.

✅ Quick workflow for you

git checkout backend-api
git add .
git commit -m "backend update"
git push origin backend-api


💡 Small tip for your multi-agent hackathon project:
Use branches like:

backend-api
frontend-ui
ai-agents
database


This keeps the repo clean and conflict-free.





